    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## The norms on $\\mathbb{R}^n$ are equivalent\n\nIn finite dimensions, all norms induce the same topology (same open sets, same convergent sequences, same continuity). The Euclidean ($\\ell^2$), Manhattan ($\\ell^1$), and supremum ($\\ell^\\infty$) norms produce different *shapes* of unit ball but agree on what's \"near\".\n\n$$\\|x\\|_1 = \\sum |x_i|, \\quad \\|x\\|_2 = \\sqrt{\\sum x_i^2}, \\quad \\|x\\|_\\infty = \\max |x_i|.$$\n",
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "theta_grid : np_to_list(np_linspace(0, 2*float(%pi), 400))$\nb2_x : map(lambda([t], cos(t)), theta_grid)$\nb2_y : map(lambda([t], sin(t)), theta_grid)$\n\n/* l^infty unit ball: square [-1, 1]^2 */\nbinf_x : [-1, 1, 1, -1, -1]$\nbinf_y : [-1, -1, 1, 1, -1]$\n\n/* l^1 unit ball: diamond |x|+|y|<=1 */\nb1_x : [1, 0, -1, 0, 1]$\nb1_y : [0, 1, 0, -1, 0]$\n\nax_draw2d(\n  color=\"blue\", line_width=2, name=\"ℓ² (Euclidean)\",\n  lines(b2_x, b2_y),\n  color=\"green\", line_width=2, name=\"ℓ¹ (Manhattan)\",\n  lines(b1_x, b1_y),\n  color=\"red\", line_width=2, name=\"ℓ^∞ (sup)\",\n  lines(binf_x, binf_y),\n  title=\"Unit balls of three equivalent norms on ℝ²\",\n  xlabel=\"x₁\", ylabel=\"x₂\",\n  grid=true, aspect_ratio=true, showlegend=true\n)$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 32,
      "outputs": [
        {
